# Windows authoring, Ubuntu CI, a public mirror. Without a declared policy the
# line endings are whatever each clone's core.autocrlf happens to be, which is
# why a file nobody edited can sit in `git status` indefinitely.
#
# Normalise every text file to LF in the repository and in the working tree.
# Everything here is Markdown, Python, JSON, YAML or BibTeX; none of it wants
# CRLF, and .githooks/pre-push is a shell script that would break with it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Figures are the one place a stray newline is unrecoverable rather than
# cosmetic: a TIFF or PDF mangled by end-of-line translation is a desk reject.
# Declared ahead of the files themselves so the rule is in place before the
# first render lands.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.tif   binary
*.tiff  binary
*.eps   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.docx  binary
